6. The Frontier Professional Education Model

6.1 Design Philosophy

The Lunar University model is mission‑driven and frontier‑oriented, grounded in heutagogy, work‑integrated learning, and competency‑based progression. It is designed to be instantiable within existing institutions.

6.2 Spiral Curriculum with Domain Tracks

A four‑year spiral revisits competencies at increasing complexity.

Year 1 – Foundations: Epistemology of AI and Professional Practice; Programming, Algorithms, Systems Theory; Control Systems; Ethics of Autonomous Technology.
Year 2 – Integration: Multi‑Agent Systems; Formal Verification and Model Checking; Alignment Theory and Constraint Formalisation; Digital Twins and Simulation; Supervised Practice I: shield design and stress‑testing.
Year 3 – Advanced Practice: Human‑AI Institutional Co‑Design; Adversarial Testing; Risk Engineering and Cascading Failure Analysis; Strategic Leadership; Professional Practice Immersion.
Year 4 – Mastery and Contribution: Capstone project designing, deploying, and formally verifying an alignment stack with documented graceful degradation; mentoring; Comprehensive Portfolio Assessment; Transition to Practice and Oath Ceremony.

6.3 The Professional Oath

I will design autonomous systems that remain accountable to humanity. I will prioritise safety over optimisation, transparency over opacity, and resilience over short‑term efficiency. I will recognise that every autonomous system participates in shaping civilisation. I accept responsibility for the consequences of the systems I create. My first duty is the preservation and flourishing of human life.

6.4 Relationship to Adjacent AI Governance Professions

The OAE works within a broader ecology: the AI Behavioral Auditor detects drift; the Architect of Human–AI Ecosystems designs institutional structures; the Human–AI Dispute Judge resolves conflicts; the Planetary Digital Twin Curator builds simulation environments; the Civilisational Risk Architect identifies existential threats. The OAE’s unique role is to embed behavioural guarantees into the architecture itself.

6.5 Economic and Societal Value

A recognised OAE profession would reduce failure rates of high‑stakes autonomous systems, provide clear liability chains, and enable accurate workforce planning. Marginal improvements in critical infrastructure AI safety could prevent economic losses in the billions.

